# Copy this file to .env.local and fill in real values.
# .env.local is git-ignored and must never be committed.
#
# SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY is SERVER-ONLY and must stay that way: it
# bypasses Row Level Security. SUPABASE_URL is likewise server-only. The
# NEXT_PUBLIC_* pair below is intentionally browser-exposed (the anon key
# is designed to be public - RLS is what protects data); several modules
# read them directly (lib/supabase-browser.ts, lib/supabase-session-server.ts,
# proxy.ts).
#
# The MoMo ingestion endpoint a user's iPhone Shortcut posts to is
# DERIVED from the Supabase URL - `<that host>/functions/v1/ingest-momo`
# (web/lib/ingest.ts, surfaced on Settings -> Connections). There is no
# separate env var for it. See docs/momo-ingest-contract.md.

SUPABASE_URL=https://zttxsaiywkfrbdxgzbjd.supabase.co
SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=https://zttxsaiywkfrbdxgzbjd.supabase.co
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=

# iPhone Shortcut setup guide (Settings -> Connections -> Set up a device,
# web/app/settings/connections/setup, web/lib/shortcut-guide.ts). Both
# optional - the guide renders fine with neither.
#   MOMO_SMS_SENDER - the real MTN Rwanda MoMo SMS sender ID to match in
#     the automation's trigger. Until set, the guide shows a
#     "<MTN sender - confirm on device>" placeholder.
#   NEXT_PUBLIC_MOMO_SHORTCUT_URL - the "Connect to OneLedger" iCloud share
#     link, if published. When set, the legacy guide shows a "Get the
#     ready-made Shortcut" button and the pairing wizard + the public /pair
#     handoff page show an "Add Connect to OneLedger" link. Browser-exposed.
#   NEXT_PUBLIC_MOMO_CAPTURE_SHORTCUT_URL - the "OneLedger Capture" iCloud
#     share link, published separately (sharing two Shortcuts as one iCloud
#     link isn't supported on every iOS version). When set alongside
#     NEXT_PUBLIC_MOMO_SHORTCUT_URL, the pairing wizard + /pair handoff show
#     a second "Add OneLedger Capture" button/link. Browser-exposed.
#   NEXT_PUBLIC_ANDROID_COMPANION_URL - a Play listing / signed APK link for
#     the OneLedger Companion Android app (android/, ADR 0010). When set, the
#     pairing wizard's "Android phone" branch and the /pair handoff show a
#     "Get the OneLedger Companion app" button. Browser-exposed. Optional -
#     the Android guide renders without it.
MOMO_SMS_SENDER=
NEXT_PUBLIC_MOMO_SHORTCUT_URL=
NEXT_PUBLIC_MOMO_CAPTURE_SHORTCUT_URL=
NEXT_PUBLIC_ANDROID_COMPANION_URL=

# Device pairing v2 (ADR 0008, docs/device-pairing.md). The `capture` Edge
# Function lets an iPhone exchange a one-time pairing token for its own
# scoped credential - no user-visible key. These are Edge Function secrets
# (supabase secrets set / Dashboard), NOT web env, and are listed here only
# as a map. Both default OFF/derived; the legacy x-ingest-key path is
# unaffected.
#   DEVICE_PAIRING_V2 - exact "enabled" turns the /capture endpoint on AND
#     shows the web pairing wizard (/integrations/connections/pair + the
#     "Connect a phone" CTA; the manual form moves under "Advanced"). The
#     wizard's first step picks iPhone or Android phone. The web
#     app reads this same var, so set it in Vercel env too, not only as an
#     Edge secret. Anything else (incl. unset) -> endpoint 404s, wizard route
#     redirects, Connections page unchanged.
#   ONELEDGER_CAPTURE_BASE_URL - stable public base returned to paired
#     devices as capture_url, e.g. https://api.oneledger.me/v1 . Unset ->
#     the function reports its own Supabase Functions URL, so provisioning
#     the subdomain later needs no device reconfiguration.
# The cleanup tick POST /api/cron/expire-pairing-sessions reuses
# REPORT_CRON_SECRET (below).
#   RAW_EVENTS_PROCESSOR_SECRET - Edge Function secret (>= 32 chars,
#     `openssl rand -hex 32`) for the process-raw-events worker that turns
#     captured evidence into transactions (docs/ingestion-pipeline.md).
#     Presented in the X-Processor-Secret header; the worker is a no-op
#     without it AND without DEVICE_PAIRING_V2=enabled. Schedule:
#     supabase/scheduling/activate_raw_events_processor.sql.

# Onboarding checklist (the "Finish setting up" dashboard nudge +
# /get-started walkthrough + the post-signup redirect there).
# web/lib/onboarding.ts / getOnboardingState in web/lib/queries.ts.
# Same convention as the Pay/Reports flags: ON unless the exact string
# "false", with an optional comma-separated workspace allowlist for a
# staged rollout. When off (or a workspace isn't on the allowlist),
# /get-started redirects to the dashboard and no nudge is shown.
ONBOARDING_CHECKLIST_ENABLED=
ONBOARDING_CHECKLIST_WORKSPACE_ALLOWLIST=

# The one canonical URL every Server Action builds links against
# (lib/site-url.ts) - signup confirmation, password reset, invites.
# Deliberately not derived from the request's origin, so a link is
# always correct regardless of which hostname the app happened to be
# reached through. Production must be the real domain, not the raw
# Vercel deployment URL.
SITE_URL=http://localhost:3417

# Resend (lib/resend.ts, lib/emails.ts) - server-only. Get your key from
# https://resend.com/api-keys and replace the placeholder below with it.
RESEND_API_KEY=re_xxxxxxxxx

# Edge Function scheduler authentication for send-notifications. Generate a
# separate high-entropy value and send it in x-notification-cron-secret.
# Never reuse SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY or REPORT_CRON_SECRET.
NOTIFICATION_CRON_SECRET=

# The "from" address for invite/security emails. Resend's sandbox sender
# (onboarding@resend.dev) only delivers to your own verified Resend
# account email - it silently fails for real invitees. Verify a domain
# in Resend (e.g. oneledger.me) and put an address on it here.
#
# Full production checklist + the GET /api/health/email operator check:
# docs/email-deliverability.md. Locally, mail is caught by inbucket at
# http://127.0.0.1:54324 - real Resend isn't hit unless a real key is set.
RESEND_FROM_EMAIL=notifications@oneledger.me

# Shared secret the Scheduled Financial Reporting engine's cron-invoked
# routes require in an X-Report-Cron-Secret header (app/api/cron/*) -
# server-only. Not yet wired to an actual scheduler (see
# app/api/cron/generate-reports/route.ts's own comment) - required for any
# manual/authenticated invocation of that route today. Generate a long
# random value (e.g. `openssl rand -hex 32`); never reuse
# SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY or any other secret for this. Must match the
# value stored in Vault when supabase/scheduling/activate_report_scheduler.sql
# is eventually run - see that file's own comments.
REPORT_CRON_SECRET=

# Operational kill switches for the reporting engine (lib/report-generation.ts,
# lib/report-delivery.ts). Both default to enabled - omit entirely, or set
# to anything other than the literal string "false", to leave them on. Set
# to "false" to pause without touching pg_cron or any report data:
#   REPORT_GENERATION_ENABLED=false      - no new reports are generated;
#                                           already-generated ones are untouched.
#   REPORT_EMAIL_DELIVERY_ENABLED=false  - no emails are sent; reports keep
#                                           generating and stay viewable in-app.
REPORT_GENERATION_ENABLED=
REPORT_EMAIL_DELIVERY_ENABLED=

# Pay & Services (Phase 1: Verified USSD Hub) - server-authoritative
# gating (lib/pay/gate.ts). Same convention as the report kill switches
# above: "on" unless the value is the exact string "false". Enforced in
# every Pay/USSD server action and query, not just the UI - setting a
# flag to "false" blocks the backend, not merely a hidden button.
#   PAY_SERVICES_ENABLED=false    - hides the global Pay action + launcher
#                                    and disables every Pay/USSD action.
#   USSD_DIRECTORY_ENABLED=false  - disables the USSD directory
#                                    specifically (Pay launcher can still
#                                    open, its USSD entry point is gone).
# PAY_SERVICES_WORKSPACE_ALLOWLIST - optional comma-separated workspace
#   ids for a staged beta. Empty/unset = every workspace. When non-empty,
#   only the listed workspaces see the surface (applies to both flags).
PAY_SERVICES_ENABLED=
USSD_DIRECTORY_ENABLED=
PAY_SERVICES_WORKSPACE_ALLOWLIST=

# Pay & Services - Phase P (payment networks). Same "on unless 'false'"
# convention, all under USSD_DIRECTORY_ENABLED + the allowlist.
#   PAYMENT_NETWORKS_ENABLED=false     - hides the public eKash network
#                                       pages, route finder, and route
#                                       result (/pay/networks/**).
#   DIRECTORY_ADMIN_ENABLED=false      - disables the /admin/directory
#                                       surface and every directory admin
#                                       RPC action wrapper.
# DIRECTORY_SUGGESTIONS_ENABLED - OPT-IN (off unless exactly "true"): the
#   user "suggest a code / route" intake (/pay/suggest). Ships behind
#   moderation tooling being operational (rollout step 6).
PAYMENT_NETWORKS_ENABLED=
DIRECTORY_ADMIN_ENABLED=
DIRECTORY_SUGGESTIONS_ENABLED=

# Pay & Services - Phase 2a (Assisted Quick Pay). Same "on unless the
# value is exactly 'false'" convention. Each is downstream of
# PAY_SERVICES_ENABLED + the allowlist above, and enforced in every
# server action / RPC, not just the UI.
#   ASSISTED_PAY_ENABLED=false        - the launcher's payment actions
#                                        revert to "coming later"; /pay/new/*
#                                        and the draft/handoff actions refuse.
#   PAYMENT_TEMPLATES_ENABLED=false   - disables /pay/templates + its actions.
#   TRUSTED_RECIPIENTS_ENABLED=false  - disables /pay/recipients + its actions.
ASSISTED_PAY_ENABLED=
PAYMENT_TEMPLATES_ENABLED=
TRUSTED_RECIPIENTS_ENABLED=

# Draft/attempt time-to-live in hours (default 24). After this, an
# initiated / awaiting-verification intent shows as Expired (lazily in
# the UI, and authoritatively once the expiry cron tick is activated -
# supabase/scheduling/activate_payment_intent_expiry.sql).
PAYMENT_INTENT_TTL_HOURS=

# How recent (minutes) a session must be before the review screen stops
# showing the "you signed in a while ago" soft notice (default 60).
# Phase 2a never BLOCKS on this - it's advisory only. A password-reentry
# step-up gate is deferred to Phase 3.
PAYMENT_SESSION_FRESHNESS_MINUTES=

# Pay & Services - Phase 2b (SMS-to-intent reconciliation & ledger
# linking). OPT-IN: OFF unless set to the exact string "true" (unlike the
# other Pay flags which are on unless "false") - it's a new,
# ledger-adjacent capability that ships behind an accuracy review.
# Reconciliation LINKS an already-ingested transaction to its intent; it
# never creates a second ledger row.
#
#   SMS_RECONCILIATION_ENABLED=true  - turns on the ingest-momo hook, the
#                                      on-handoff match, and the retry cron.
#   SMS_RECONCILIATION_MODE=observe  - (default) record candidate links on
#                                      /pay/reconciliation for review; do
#                                      NOT mutate the intent or the ledger.
#   SMS_RECONCILIATION_MODE=apply    - link + verify automatically once a
#                                      deterministic match is found.
#
# BOTH vars must ALSO be set as Supabase edge-function secrets (not just
# Vercel env) for the ingest-momo hook to see them:
#   supabase secrets set SMS_RECONCILIATION_ENABLED=true SMS_RECONCILIATION_MODE=observe
SMS_RECONCILIATION_ENABLED=
SMS_RECONCILIATION_MODE=

# Pay & Services - Scan to pay (Phases R1-R2). OPT-IN: OFF unless set to
# the exact string "true" (same convention as SMS_RECONCILIATION_ENABLED).
# Downstream of PAY_SERVICES_ENABLED + the workspace allowlist. Ships in
# stages:
#   R1 - camera scanner shell (rear camera, full permission/failure
#        matrix, guaranteed stream teardown).
#   R2 - QR decode (native BarcodeDetector; camera + local image upload)
#        and server-side payload classification against the verified USSD
#        directory + provider allowlist.
#   R3 - review screen + external hand-off for VERIFIED USSD codes:
#        creates a payment_intents draft (source='qr_scan') and opens the
#        tel: instruction on an explicit tap. Never claims settlement.
#        (provider links / OneLedger / EMV codes are shown but not yet
#        actionable.)
#   R4 - a qr_scan intent reconciles + expires through the existing
#        Phase 2b machinery unchanged; its lifecycle surface (/pay/[id],
#        activity, confirm/cancel) is available on assisted OR scan.
#   R5 - analytics (redacting trackScanEvent, no sink), monitoring
#        (logScanError, [scan-error] prefix), and the device-QA /
#        rollout runbook (docs/pay-scan-verification-runbook.md).
#   R-oneledger - a OneLedger merchant-payment scan (RWF) is mapped onto
#        the seeded (published, UNVERIFIED) MTN pay-merchant USSD code
#        and handed off like a USSD scan; the user types the amount when
#        the payload omits it.
#   SCAN_TO_PAY_ENABLED=true  - shows the "Scan to pay" launcher entry.
SCAN_TO_PAY_ENABLED=

# OneLedger Spaces (household collaboration) - lib/spaces/gate.ts.
# OPT-IN, same convention as SCAN_TO_PAY_ENABLED: the household surface
# (create a household, share a source into a Space, per-member
# attribution, household notification prefs) is OFF unless this is
# exactly "true". A disabled flag blocks the server actions, not just the
# buttons. Statement import, the notifications inbox, and duplicate
# review are NOT gated by this - they work for personal workspaces too.
#   SPACES_ENABLED=true             - turns the household surface on.
#   SPACES_WORKSPACE_ALLOWLIST      - optional comma-separated workspace
#     ids; when non-empty, ONLY those workspaces see it (staged beta).
SPACES_ENABLED=
SPACES_WORKSPACE_ALLOWLIST=

# Experience modes (ADR 0011) - lib/experience-mode/gate.ts. The mode
# (Personal / Household / Business) is derived from the active Space's
# kind and decides which surfaces are VISIBLE - it is never an
# authorization check. The Business-only surfaces (Bills, reconciliation
# centre, accounting connectors, developer platform) are dark until this
# is exactly "true"; an organization Space otherwise shows the Household
# surface set. Personal/Household modes are always on and need no flag.
#   EXPERIENCE_MODE_BUSINESS_ENABLED=true   - lights up the Business surfaces.
#   EXPERIENCE_MODE_BUSINESS_ALLOWLIST     - optional comma-separated
#     workspace ids; when non-empty, ONLY those see the Business surfaces.
EXPERIENCE_MODE_BUSINESS_ENABLED=
EXPERIENCE_MODE_BUSINESS_ALLOWLIST=

# Onboarding milestone journey (ADR 0012) - lib/onboarding/journey.ts.
# The persisted-spine + intent step of the redesigned first-run flow.
# OFF unless exactly "true"; while off, /onboarding/intent redirects to
# the existing /get-started flow and nothing new is shown. The migration
# (20261129000000) is additive and the reader degrades gracefully, so
# this can be flipped independently of the Supabase deploy.
ONBOARDING_JOURNEY_ENABLED=

# Financial intelligence (ADR 0014) - lib/intelligence/*. Deterministic,
# explainable insights on Home: a conservative cash-flow forecast (known
# vs estimated kept separate), a spending-baseline comparison, and
# detected recurring payments - each with a "Why am I seeing this?"
# disclosure. OFF unless exactly "true"; when off, Home makes no extra
# queries. No invented scores, no new charts, AI never computes a value.
INTELLIGENCE_ENABLED=

# Account deletion (ADR 0016) - lib/account-deletion.ts. Lets a user
# schedule permanent deletion of their own account with a 30-day grace
# window (request_account_deletion / cancel_account_deletion,
# 20261201000000). OFF unless exactly "true"; when off, /settings/privacy/
# data still offers data export (always free) but hides the delete flow.
# The irreversible erasure (execute_account_deletion) is a separate
# follow-up and is not wired even when this is on.
ACCOUNT_DELETION_ENABLED=

# Optional AI report commentary ("OneLedger Insights", lib/ai/*) -
# server-only, entirely optional. A user only gets AI commentary if BOTH
# their own report_preferences.include_ai_analysis is on AND a key below
# is configured - missing either degrades silently to no commentary,
# never an error, and the deterministic report is unaffected either way.
#
# AI_PROVIDER selects which SDK is used ("anthropic", the default, or
# "openai") - a config change, not a code change. AI_MODEL overrides the
# default model for whichever provider is selected. Bills & Expenses
# extraction (below) also honours "mock" here for a keyless deterministic
# response in local dev / e2e.
AI_PROVIDER=anthropic
AI_MODEL=
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=
OPENAI_API_KEY=

# Integrations area (imports, exports, connections, sync, activity) -
# lib/integrations/gate.ts. Same convention as PAY_SERVICES_ENABLED: the
# switch vars are ON unless exactly "false"; the allowlist narrows a
# staged beta; INTEGRATIONS_SYNC_ENABLED is OFF unless exactly "true".
# A disabled flag blocks the server routes/actions, not just the nav link.
#   INTEGRATIONS_ENABLED=false            - hides the nav entry and blocks
#     every /integrations route and integration action.
#   INTEGRATIONS_WORKSPACE_ALLOWLIST      - optional comma-separated
#     workspace ids; when non-empty, ONLY those workspaces see the area.
#   INTEGRATIONS_IMPORT_STUDIO_ENABLED=false - disables just the Import
#     Studio (/integrations/imports).
#   INTEGRATIONS_EXPORT_CENTER_ENABLED=false - disables just the Export
#     Center (/integrations/exports) and its job cron.
#   INTEGRATIONS_SYNC_ENABLED=true        - opt-in; turns on Sync &
#     Automation (/integrations/sync) and scheduled deliveries.
# Phase 2 (all downstream of INTEGRATIONS_SYNC_ENABLED):
#   INTEGRATIONS_DESTINATIONS_ENABLED=false - disables just the
#     Destinations surface (download + signed webhook delivery). On
#     unless "false".
#   INTEGRATIONS_WORKBOOKS_ENABLED=true   - opt-in; Connected Workbooks +
#     conflict review. OFF unless exactly "true".
#   INTEGRATIONS_CLOUD_STORAGE_ENABLED=true - opt-in; the cloud-storage
#     destination type. A provider is additionally dark until its OAuth
#     client env below is set.
#   GOOGLE_DRIVE_CLIENT_ID / GOOGLE_DRIVE_CLIENT_SECRET,
#   MICROSOFT_CLIENT_ID / MICROSOFT_CLIENT_SECRET,
#   DROPBOX_APP_KEY / DROPBOX_APP_SECRET - absent => that provider stays
#     dark and its OAuth routes return 501.
# Phase 3:
#   INTEGRATIONS_RECONCILIATION_CENTER_ENABLED=false - disables just the
#     Reconciliation Center (/integrations/reconciliation), a read-only hub
#     over the existing review queues. On unless "false".
#   BALANCE_RECONCILIATION_ENABLED=true - lets the
#     /api/cron/run-balance-reconciliation route forward a sweep to the
#     reconcile-balances Edge Function (opt-in, exact "true"). The function
#     ALSO needs its own project secret to do anything:
#       supabase secrets set BALANCE_RECONCILIATION_ENABLED=enabled
#     (exact "enabled"; hard-404s otherwise). Populates balance_reconciliations
#     for the Reconciliation Center's "balance drift" section. Not
#     scheduler-wired - schedule it in the Dashboard or via pg_cron.
#   INTEGRATIONS_ACCOUNTANT_PACKAGE_ENABLED=false - disables just the
#     "Ready for Accountant" package (/integrations/accountant + the
#     build-accountant-packages cron). On unless "false". Small packages
#     build inline in the create action; the cron (REPORT_CRON_SECRET) only
#     handles large / stuck ones and retention purge, and is not
#     scheduler-wired.
#   INTEGRATIONS_ACCOUNTING_CONNECTORS_ENABLED=true - opt-in (exact
#     "true"), downstream of INTEGRATIONS_SYNC_ENABLED. Turns on the
#     `accounting` destination type + connected ledgers.
#   QUICKBOOKS_CLIENT_ID / QUICKBOOKS_CLIENT_SECRET,
#   XERO_CLIENT_ID / XERO_CLIENT_SECRET,
#   ZOHO_BOOKS_CLIENT_ID / ZOHO_BOOKS_CLIENT_SECRET,
#   ODOO_CLIENT_ID / ODOO_CLIENT_SECRET - absent => that accounting
#     provider stays dark and its OAuth routes return 501.
# Phase 4 (Developer Platform):
#   INTEGRATIONS_DEVELOPER_API_ENABLED=true - opt-in (exact "true"): the
#     read-only /api/v1 REST surface + /integrations/developer key screen.
#     First non-session public surface; every route is bearer-key-auth'd,
#     scoped, rate-limited and request-logged.
#   INTEGRATIONS_WEBHOOKS_DEV_ENABLED=true - opt-in (exact "true"),
#     downstream of the developer API: outbound webhook subscriptions +
#     the deliver-webhooks cron.
#   INTEGRATIONS_MARKETPLACE_ENABLED=false - disables the
#     /integrations/marketplace catalog. On unless "false".
#   API_RATE_LIMIT_PER_MINUTE - per-key read rate cap (default 120).
INTEGRATIONS_ENABLED=
INTEGRATIONS_WORKSPACE_ALLOWLIST=
INTEGRATIONS_IMPORT_STUDIO_ENABLED=
INTEGRATIONS_EXPORT_CENTER_ENABLED=
INTEGRATIONS_SYNC_ENABLED=
INTEGRATIONS_DESTINATIONS_ENABLED=
INTEGRATIONS_WORKBOOKS_ENABLED=
INTEGRATIONS_CLOUD_STORAGE_ENABLED=
INTEGRATIONS_RECONCILIATION_CENTER_ENABLED=
BALANCE_RECONCILIATION_ENABLED=
INTEGRATIONS_ACCOUNTANT_PACKAGE_ENABLED=
INTEGRATIONS_ACCOUNTING_CONNECTORS_ENABLED=
GOOGLE_DRIVE_CLIENT_ID=
GOOGLE_DRIVE_CLIENT_SECRET=
MICROSOFT_CLIENT_ID=
MICROSOFT_CLIENT_SECRET=
DROPBOX_APP_KEY=
DROPBOX_APP_SECRET=
QUICKBOOKS_CLIENT_ID=
QUICKBOOKS_CLIENT_SECRET=
XERO_CLIENT_ID=
XERO_CLIENT_SECRET=
ZOHO_BOOKS_CLIENT_ID=
ZOHO_BOOKS_CLIENT_SECRET=
ODOO_CLIENT_ID=
ODOO_CLIENT_SECRET=
INTEGRATIONS_DEVELOPER_API_ENABLED=
INTEGRATIONS_WEBHOOKS_DEV_ENABLED=
INTEGRATIONS_MARKETPLACE_ENABLED=
API_RATE_LIMIT_PER_MINUTE=

# Bills & Expenses (Invoice & Expense Processor) - server-authoritative
# gating (lib/bills/gate.ts). This is a NEW, ledger-adjacent capability,
# so - like SCAN_TO_PAY_ENABLED / SMS_RECONCILIATION_ENABLED - it is
# OPT-IN: every flag here is OFF unless the value is the exact string
# "true". Enforced in every /bills action, API route and RPC wrapper, not
# just the UI.
#   BILLS_ENABLED=true              - the whole Bills & Expenses surface
#                                    (/bills, upload, the API routes).
#                                    Unset/anything-but-"true" = /bills is
#                                    notFound() and every action refuses.
#   BILLS_EXTRACTION_ENABLED=true   - Phase 2 AI classification +
#                                    structured extraction worker
#                                    (/api/cron/process-bill-documents).
#                                    Uses AI_PROVIDER above: "anthropic"
#                                    (default, PDF + images), "openai"
#                                    (images only), or "mock" (a
#                                    deterministic invoice, no key -
#                                    local dev / e2e). OFF unless "true".
#   BILLS_AUTO_APPROVAL_ENABLED     - DARK. Architected-for only (master
#                                    prompt §2); never honoured in the
#                                    first release. Leave unset.
# BILLS_WORKSPACE_ALLOWLIST - optional comma-separated workspace ids for a
#   staged internal beta. Empty/unset = every workspace (once BILLS_ENABLED
#   is "true"). When non-empty, only the listed workspaces see the surface.
BILLS_ENABLED=
BILLS_EXTRACTION_ENABLED=
BILLS_AUTO_APPROVAL_ENABLED=
BILLS_WORKSPACE_ALLOWLIST=

# Bills & Expenses - upload limits (master prompt §5). Safe defaults apply
# if unset or non-numeric.
#   BILLS_MAX_UPLOAD_BYTES      - per-file size cap. Default 15728640 (15 MiB).
#   BILLS_MAX_PAGE_COUNT        - per-PDF page cap. Default 25.
#   BILLS_SIGNED_URL_TTL_SECONDS - lifetime of an original/preview signed
#                                  URL. Default 300 (5 min).
BILLS_MAX_UPLOAD_BYTES=15728640
BILLS_MAX_PAGE_COUNT=25
BILLS_SIGNED_URL_TTL_SECONDS=300

# Bills & Expenses - Phase 8 rollout.
#   BILLS_NOTIFICATIONS_ENABLED=true - the extraction worker emails
#       workspace reviewers "a document is ready for review" (link only,
#       no supplier/amount/OCR text). OFF unless exactly "true"; needs
#       RESEND_API_KEY + RESEND_FROM_EMAIL (above). De-duped per document.
#   BILL_WORKER_BATCH_SIZE          - documents processed per cron tick.
#       Default 5.
# The workers themselves (/api/cron/process-bill-documents,
# /api/cron/bill-monitoring) are activated by the MANUAL, one-time
# supabase/scheduling/activate_bill_workers.sql - never auto-scheduled.
BILLS_NOTIFICATIONS_ENABLED=
BILL_WORKER_BATCH_SIZE=
